# License status: UNDECIDED — no license granted

Copyright (c) 2026 Nitin Joshi. **All rights reserved.**

No open-source license has been chosen for this repository yet. Until a license is added,
no permission is granted to use, copy, modify, or distribute this software, and the default
"all rights reserved" copyright applies.

## Why this file says this

Choosing a license is a deliberate legal decision. Rather than have a tool pick one on the
author's behalf, this file records that the decision is still pending.

## How to resolve it before a public release

1. Decide whether the project should be open source, and under which terms.
2. If open source, replace this file with a conventional permissive license such as
   [MIT](../) or [Apache-2.0](https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0) (Apache-2.0 also
   includes an explicit patent grant).
3. If not open source, replace this file with an explicit proprietary license.

## Third-party components

Runtime dependencies (`express`, `dotenv`) and any transitive dependencies remain under
their own licenses; see `node_modules/*/LICENSE` after `npm install`.

## Data and credentials

This repository must never contain real API keys, `.env` files, SQLite databases, encryption
keys, or logs. Those live only on the operator's machine (see `.gitignore` and `SECURITY.md`).
